@startuml
title Meridian End-to-End Weather Reading Trace

actor "Field Station" as FS
participant "Ingest\n(C)" as ING
database "SQLite Store" as DB
participant "Analytics Orchestrator\n(Python)" as ORCH
participant "Crop Model\n(Fortran)" as MODEL
participant "Output Parser\n(Python)" as PARSER
participant "REST API\n(Java)" as API
participant "Operator Console\n(JavaScript / jQuery)" as CON

FS -> ING : 44-byte binary telemetry frame
note right of ING
Big-endian format
MRD1 header
Station ID
Year + day-of-year
TMAX, TMIN, RAIN,
SRAD, RH, WIND
end note

ING -> DB : INSERT OR REPLACE reading
note right of DB
SQLite reading row
stnid, year, doy,
tmax, tmin, rain,
srad, rh, wind, flags
end note

DB --> ORCH : SELECT weather readings
note right of ORCH
SQL rows converted to
Python Reading objects
end note

ORCH -> MODEL : MERIDIAN.DAT
note right of MODEL
Fixed-width text deck
DOY, TMAX, TMIN,
RAIN, SRAD
end note

MODEL --> PARSER : MERIDIAN.OUT
note right of PARSER
Fixed-width text output
DOY, SW, ET,
DRAIN, BIOM, LAI
end note

PARSER -> DB : INSERT forecast data
note right of DB
SQLite forecast and
forecast_daily rows
end note

CON -> API : GET /api/series?station=ID&year=YYYY
note over CON, API
HTTP GET request
Query parameters:
station, year
end note

API -> DB : SELECT forecast_daily rows
DB --> API : SQLite query result

API --> CON : HTTP 200 application/json
note right of CON
JSON array of forecast objects
end note

CON -> CON : Parse JSON into JavaScript objects
CON -> CON : Format numeric value
CON -> CON : Render HTML DOM / bar chart

@enduml